+# Live compatibility research
+
+Accessed 2026-08-14. The local snapshot remains the implementation and grading authority.
+
+- **Correlating VMware Cloud Foundation version with the versions of its constituent products** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article?legacyId=52520 — Used to confirm the VCF 5.2.2 build and its vCenter 8.0 U3g, ESXi 8.0 U3g, and NSX 4.2.3 bill of materials.
+- **Using the VMware Product Interoperability Matrixes** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/343230 — Used to confirm how Broadcom publishes component interoperability and patch-level upgrade-path results, including the need to expose patch and legacy releases when checking a hop.
+- **Product Interoperability Matrix** — https://interopmatrix.broadcom.com/Upgrade — Used to check the patch-level vCenter and ESXi source-to-target paths represented in the pinned snapshot rather than inferring support from version-number ordering.
+- **Upgrade vCenter Server 7.0 to 8.0** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/372863 — Used to confirm the supported major-version upgrade direction for the existing workload vCenter and that product compatibility must be checked before the transition.
+- **Install or upgrade ESXi from 7.x to 8.x** — https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/390293/install-or-upgrade-esxi-from-7x-to-8x.html — Used to confirm that vCenter must reach its target before the workload ESXi hosts are upgraded.
+- **Introduction to the VMware Cloud Foundation (VCF) Import Tool** — https://blogs.vmware.com/cloud-foundation/2024/09/11/introduction-to-the-vmware-cloud-foundation-vcf-import-tool/ — Used to confirm that an existing SDDC Manager at VCF 5.2.x can import an additional vCenter as a VI workload domain, with inventory checks before the import and NSX deployment as part of the workflow.
+
+No consulted live source conflicted with the pinned compatibility facts used by `migration-plan.json`.
